{"step_index":161,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-18T07:38:30Z","input_tokens":3131,"cache_read_tokens":263547,"output_tokens":3378,"thinking":"The timing suggests reusable Spider-Verse assets are already built in `env-2` and `anim` environments. Shader, texture, and compositor nodes from those builds could be leveraged. The presence of these files indicates potential for significant optimization.\n\n\nThe existing assets offer a foundation for a new 3D circuit (\"V7 / V6-Ultra\"). The user's feedback (\"not satisfied with the circuit design,\" \"not enough sense of the lens,\" \"rendering effects are not good,\" \"more impact\") necessitates a redesign with enhanced cinematography and a high-impact render system. A new worker dedicated to the 3D circuit generator is needed to pursue this. The architecture must be non-colliding, split into 4 pieces.\n\n\nThe existing V6 architecture can be cleanly upgraded by redesigning it as a \"V6 Spider-Verse Mega-Circuit\". A new `track` engineer is needed because `env-2` and `anim` are completing their turns and the circuit design requires computation of 3D elevation, banked turns, and other dynamic properties. The goal is a shorter, denser, and more action-packed circuit, leveraging Spider-Verse assets for maximum visual impact.\n\n\nThe initial 5.8 km lap's object density was too low, resulting in large empty spaces between assets. Reducing the circuit to approximately 3.4–3.8 km allows for a significant increase in architectural and prop density, potentially tripling the objects per meter. This tighter design will necessitate continuous set-pieces every six seconds, eliminating flat, uninteresting sections.\n\n\nInitial design concepts incorporate intense visuals: a steep uphill S-crest, a suspended sky-bridge above a neon harbor, and a Laguna-Seca-style corkscrew plunge. These elements increase the overall circuit's visual dynamism, with a goal of cinematic impact. The revised layout will conclude with an acoustic neon strobe tunnel followed by a high-speed harbor finish.\n\n\nThe circuit design aims for cinematic impact with a rapid visual rhythm. The harbor section now features intense braking effects culminating in a wet, mirror-slick finish. Optimizations target reducing render time by half, enabling more iterations and higher quality final output.\n\nThe render look of earlier versions needs addressing. A major change is enabling ray tracing for a neon-lit, wet asphalt surface. The new surface will incorporate puddle maps and reflections, with modifications to the initial grass model.\n\n\nThe revised circuit design will leverage neon reflections on a wet road surface to achieve a dramatic visual impact, with posterization effects for an *Across the Spider-Verse* aesthetic. Incorporating a 3D track ribbon with elevation and superelevation banking enables a more dynamic racing line with enhanced realism.\n\nMonumental set-pieces, like a Megacity Skyscraper Canyon and a Cable-Stayed Suspension Sky-Bridge, will use a combination of procedural comic skyscraper elements and overhead structures to generate high-impact silhouettes and parallax effects, increasing visual drama.\n\n\nThe harbor design includes monumental H-frame towers with glowing cables reflecting a city skyline, enhancing visual depth. A 450m enclosed neon strobe tunnel will utilize closely spaced light ribs to create intense light-band strobing effects.\n\nFaux-volumetric god-ray light shafts and upgraded car FX, including afterburner shock diamonds and titanium spark showers, will be implemented for cinematic impact.\n\n\nThe previous camera setups lacked dynamic impact, resembling static TV cameras. The approach now focuses on redesigned, high-energy shots with rapid cuts synchronized to the music's beat, aiming for a cinematic feel.\n\nThis redesign involves full 3D attitude coupling where the camera rigs accurately respond to the track's elevation changes and banking. The new workflow also includes anamorphic widescreen framing with cinematic scope bars for a dynamic comic frame look.\n\n\nFocus is now on camera rig design for maximum visual impact. The approach is to create a dynamic series of shots, each with its own specific feel and function within the visual narrative. Each shot's setup will have specific focal length, and Dutch roll.\nThe goal is to incorporate a variety of extreme camera angles and movements, synchronized with sound design, for an intense cinematic experience. The revised cinematography will utilize the track, lighting, and visual elements to enhance dynamic action.\n\n\nCamera work will feature quick pan transitions and dramatic two-frame black/white/crimson impact frames. A new cinema compositor will be developed, incorporating rich S-Curve AgX punch, neon bloom, and chromatic halation. This compositor (`Comp_V6_SpiderVerse`) will also feature screen-space Ben-Day halftones, Earth-65 brushstrokes, and focal-plane CMYK misregistration.\n\nThe audio and visual synchronization will be done by a dedicated script. It will read the track data to be rendered, the audio, and will synthesize custom sound effects such as the reverb from the tunnel and the titanium sparks.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"swarm","args":{"action":"status"}},{"name":"read_board","args":{"since":28}}]}
